# robonix/system/scene/goal_near — find a navigation-safe approach pose
# near a registered physical scene object. Room annotations are rejected;
# use robonix/system/scene/goal_region for regions. Map-frame (x, y, yaw); pass to
# robonix/service/navigation/navigate after.
#
# `reachable=false` when the occupancy grid has no free cell within
# the (service-side-default) search radius of the object — caller
# should pick a different target. `reason` is a short human-readable
# string for both branches.
#
# `approach_yaw` names the side of the object the pose should be taken from,
# in radians in the map frame. It only orders the candidates: the returned yaw
# always turns towards the object, and the opposite side is still returned when
# the preferred one has no footprint-safe cell, so `reachable=true` does not
# promise the requested side. `has_approach_yaw` is what says a side was named,
# because 0.0 is a real direction and a float64 cannot carry "unset". Without
# it the pose faces the robot's own approach.

string object_id
bool has_approach_yaw
float64 approach_yaw
---
bool reachable
float64 x
float64 y
float64 yaw
string reason
